IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ga-dates`
IMPORT `ga-orders`

-- Guardianship Act 1987 (NSW) -- worked cases for every exported question in ga-orders.l4.
-- Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text; none was copied from the encoding's output. Each
-- assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Dates are illustrative.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `cases -- orders about me`

`d` MEANS `the date`

`me` MEANS `I am`
`PG` MEANS `the Public Guardian`
`NSWT` MEANS `the NSW Trustee`
`manager` MEANS `the manager of my estate`
`guardian` MEANS `my guardian`
`concerned` MEANS `someone the Tribunal considers has a genuine concern for my welfare`
`stranger` MEANS `someone else`

`continuing` MEANS `a continuing order`
`temporary` MEANS `a temporary order`
`plenary` MEANS `a plenary order`
`limited` MEANS `a limited order`
`initial` MEANS `the initial order`
`renewed` MEANS `a renewed order`

`must` MEANS `the Tribunal must review it`
`may refuse` MEANS `the Tribunal may refuse to review it`
`not required` MEANS `the Tribunal is not required to review it when it expires`
`asked` MEANS `someone has asked for a review`
`ending` MEANS `the order's period is ending`

`by warrant` MEANS `under a search warrant (section 12)`
`by order` MEANS `under a Tribunal removal order (section 11)`
`not yet` MEANS `the three days have not yet passed, so section 13(2) does not yet stop the Secretary keeping me`
`in time` MEANS `the Secretary applied for a guardianship order in time, so section 13(2) does not stop the Secretary keeping me`
`too late` MEANS `the three days have passed without an application, so the Secretary must not keep me`
`no limit` MEANS `section 13(2) sets no limit, because I was removed under a Tribunal order`

`interim in force` MEANS `it is in force, pending the Tribunal's further consideration`
`interim completed` MEANS `the Tribunal completed its further consideration in time, and what follows is its decision`
`interim revoked` MEANS `it was taken to be revoked when its period expired`

§§ `s 9 -- who can apply`

-- 16 on the day of the application, and one day short.
#ASSERT `Can this person apply for a guardianship order about me` `me` (`d` 10 3 2010) (`d` 10 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can this person apply for a guardianship order about me` `me` (`d` 10 3 2010) (`d` 9 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can this person apply for a guardianship order about me` `PG` (`d` 1 1 1950) (`d` 1 6 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can this person apply for a guardianship order about me` `concerned` (`d` 1 1 1950) (`d` 1 6 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can this person apply for a guardianship order about me` `NSWT` (`d` 1 1 1950) (`d` 1 6 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can this person apply for a guardianship order about me` `stranger` (`d` 1 1 1950) (`d` 1 6 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can this person apply for a guardianship order about me` `stranger` (`d` 10 3 2010) (`d` 9 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE

